89
00:02:19,754 --> 00:02:24,354
We managed to get away safely,
 but the path out is completely blocked.

90
00:02:30,844 --> 00:02:32,514
What is this place?

91
00:02:34,814 --> 00:02:39,894
They told me that I was found,
 as a baby, in a box like this.

92
00:02:39,894 --> 00:02:41,604
You mean...

93
00:02:41,604 --> 00:02:44,024
So does House Einfolk...

94
00:02:45,404 --> 00:02:49,264
Back when my foster father was investigating the ruin in the Ymir Theocracy,

95
00:02:49,264 --> 00:02:52,584
he found me and took me in.

96
00:02:52,584 --> 00:02:56,554
As a piece of the puzzle that is
 the ruins and the lost past,

97
00:02:56,554 --> 00:02:58,414
he thought I could be useful.

98
00:02:59,714 --> 00:03:05,424
With no memory of my past,
 I lived in House Einfolk none the wiser.

99
00:03:07,994 --> 00:03:11,914
I realized at a very early age that I was adopted.

100
00:03:11,914 --> 00:03:14,634
My parents, my siblings, the servants...

101
00:03:14,634 --> 00:03:16,504
They all treated me like an outsider.

102
00:03:21,214 --> 00:03:23,824
So I worked hard.

103
00:03:23,824 --> 00:03:27,154
In my studies, in etiquette,
 in being a Drag-Knight...

104
00:03:27,154 --> 00:03:29,724
So that people would like me.

105
00:03:29,724 --> 00:03:32,054
So that I'd be accepted as part of the family.

106
00:03:33,304 --> 00:03:36,614
But I never got what I wanted most.

107
00:03:36,614 --> 00:03:40,444
I had become skilled enough to receive a Divine Raiment Machine Dragon,

108
00:03:40,444 --> 00:03:42,954
but that only alienated me
 from my siblings even further.

109
00:03:43,914 --> 00:03:49,924
I overheard them say that I really must not be entirely human.

110
00:03:51,054 --> 00:03:55,584
The reason I was so bent on exploring the ruins
 was that I didn't want to believe it.

111
00:03:55,584 --> 00:03:58,054
I wanted to believe there was
 some kind of misunderstanding

112
00:03:58,054 --> 00:04:01,184
and that I was in fact a true 
daughter of House Einfolk.

113
00:04:01,784 --> 00:04:06,244
But I guess I truly am a survivor of the ruins.

114
00:04:06,244 --> 00:04:10,484
There's no doubt now that I've seen the ruin react to me.

115
00:04:10,484 --> 00:04:14,704
But I still don't know anything about my past
 or whether there are others like me.

116
00:04:15,064 --> 00:04:19,904
B-But it's not like everything here's been
 explored, and there are other ruins out—

117
00:04:19,904 --> 00:04:21,404
I'm not exploring any more.

118
00:04:21,404 --> 00:04:21,954
What?

119
00:04:22,684 --> 00:04:25,244
I'm too afraid to go any further.

120
00:04:26,994 --> 00:04:32,564
What if I kept exploring the ruins and still never found others like me, or anyone who'd accept me?

121
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:34,774
Krulcifer...

122
00:04:35,474 --> 00:04:39,514
I'm sorry you had to listen to all that.

123
00:04:39,514 --> 00:04:41,644
And from a nobody like me.

124
00:04:41,644 --> 00:04:42,994
You're not nobody!

125
00:04:45,754 --> 00:04:49,084
The Ymir Theocracy and the
 House of Einfolk don't matter here!

126
00:04:49,084 --> 00:04:54,394
You're our fellow student and Drag-Knight,
 and my girlf—my partner!

127
00:04:54,394 --> 00:04:55,794
So please don't...

128
00:04:58,914 --> 00:05:02,394
Please don't say things like that.

129
00:05:06,274 --> 00:05:09,964
Lux, let me give you a fair warning.

130
00:05:10,534 --> 00:05:14,124
You shouldn't always believe
 a woman's sad stories.

131
00:05:14,624 --> 00:05:16,474
Was all that a lie?!

132
00:05:17,034 --> 00:05:20,654
Your only weakness is your
 excessive kindness to others.

133
00:05:20,654 --> 00:05:25,484
I wanted to see what you'd do,
 but this reaction was more than I was expecting.

134
00:05:30,144 --> 00:05:34,404
But really, how can be you so softhearted?

135
00:05:34,404 --> 00:05:37,754
You were a prince of that notorious old empire.

136
00:05:39,074 --> 00:05:41,584
That might be my fate.

137
00:05:43,574 --> 00:05:49,314
I was banished from the imperial court, along with my mother and Airi, on account of my grandfather.

138
00:05:49,314 --> 00:05:53,134
He was a teacher for the imperial family.

139
00:05:53,134 --> 00:05:57,134
But seeing the empire's ways,
 I guess he couldn't stay silent.

140
00:05:59,124 --> 00:06:00,034
However...

141
00:06:02,684 --> 00:06:05,554
Please someone help!

142
00:06:05,554 --> 00:06:07,144
My mother!

143
00:06:08,924 --> 00:06:13,404
No one would lend a hand to members of the imperial family they'd suffered under for so long.

144
00:06:16,684 --> 00:06:22,714
In the end, we were shunned and forsaken
 by both the imperial family and the people.

145
00:06:24,874 --> 00:06:26,364
What a horrible story.

146
00:06:27,364 --> 00:06:29,724
Didn't you resent them all?

147
00:06:29,724 --> 00:06:31,214
I did.

148
00:06:31,214 --> 00:06:35,294
I believed there wasn't a person in the world who'd stand by us.

149
00:06:35,294 --> 00:06:38,004
I was about to give into hatred.

150
00:06:38,004 --> 00:06:38,924
But...

151
00:06:40,084 --> 00:06:42,224
Philuffy saved me.

152
00:06:43,224 --> 00:06:48,664
She came to see me every day,
 even though I had nothing to give her.

153
00:06:48,664 --> 00:06:49,734
So it was her.

154
00:06:50,234 --> 00:06:56,164
That's when I realized that I didn't really want to hate anyone.

155
00:06:56,164 --> 00:06:57,824
The people I cared for...

156
00:06:57,824 --> 00:07:00,094
People I could come to care for...

157
00:07:00,094 --> 00:07:02,494
I didn't want to hate them
 because of the empire.

158
00:07:03,464 --> 00:07:08,634
I wanted to create a kingdom where one didn't have to hate the people they love.

159
00:07:08,634 --> 00:07:14,504
If you had become a prince of the new kingdom,
 perhaps you could have saved me too.

160
00:07:20,304 --> 00:07:21,514
What?!

161
00:07:23,894 --> 00:07:25,604
A-A drill?!

162
00:07:25,604 --> 00:07:27,014
What do you think, Lux?

163
00:07:27,014 --> 00:07:29,954
This guy's pretty useful, don't you think?

164
00:07:29,954 --> 00:07:31,524
U-Um, I guess so.

165
00:07:32,384 --> 00:07:37,274
By the way, I hope you didn't do anything to Krulcifer.

166
00:07:37,274 --> 00:07:39,534
Anything like what?

167
00:07:40,124 --> 00:07:43,794
A-Are you going to make me say it?! You dunce!

168
00:07:43,794 --> 00:07:45,254
Y-You lecher!

169
00:07:45,254 --> 00:07:46,244
What?!

170
00:07:46,244 --> 00:07:48,204
How am I a lecher?!

171
00:07:48,204 --> 00:07:49,544
You just are—

172
00:07:52,924 --> 00:07:57,924
So in the end, you couldn't
 find anything about the key.

173
00:07:58,354 --> 00:08:01,144
And you completely destroyed your Wyvern too.

174
00:08:01,144 --> 00:08:03,184
I said I was sorry.

175
00:08:03,184 --> 00:08:08,324
I'm mad at you for not learning from your past mistakes.

176
00:08:08,324 --> 00:08:11,434
You knew the ruins were dangerous,
 and you still acted recklessly.

177
00:08:12,244 --> 00:08:14,094
I'm ashamed of myself.

178
00:08:14,094 --> 00:08:16,444
So the horn wasn't the key.

179
00:08:16,444 --> 00:08:21,834
No. I held it out while inside, but there was no reaction.

180
00:08:21,834 --> 00:08:23,874
Did anything else out of the ordinary happen?

181
00:08:27,074 --> 00:08:28,944
Not really.

182
00:08:28,944 --> 00:08:30,564
I see.

183
00:08:30,564 --> 00:08:34,784
It's a pity that we made no progress,
 but we have to play the hand we're dealt.

184
00:08:35,494 --> 00:08:38,284
All right, Lux, drink this.

185
00:08:38,284 --> 00:08:39,094
What is it?

186
00:08:39,464 --> 00:08:44,094
Herbal tea. A present for you from Krulcifer.

187
00:08:44,094 --> 00:08:48,104
It eases fatigue and helps you sleep better.

188
00:08:49,034 --> 00:08:49,994
But...

189
00:08:49,994 --> 00:08:52,524
You'll still make it to the duel.

190
00:08:52,524 --> 00:08:55,104
You should get some rest before then.

191
00:08:55,104 --> 00:08:57,884
Okay. Thanks.

192
00:09:13,384 --> 00:09:16,334
Are you satisfied now, Krulcifer?

193
00:09:16,334 --> 00:09:18,424
Yes. Thank you.

194
00:09:18,424 --> 00:09:22,844
It would be wrong to drag your brother any further into my personal problems.

195
00:09:23,794 --> 00:09:26,554
His job will be over tomorrow.

196
00:09:31,524 --> 00:09:37,804
You still don't understand
 anything about my brother.

197
00:09:39,664 --> 00:09:43,584
I see you are punctual, my future wife.

198
00:09:44,114 --> 00:09:47,324
But where is the little boy?

199
00:09:47,324 --> 00:09:48,914
I sent him home.

200
00:09:48,914 --> 00:09:50,494
Is that a problem for you?

201
00:09:51,704 --> 00:09:52,944
Very well.

202
00:09:55,914 --> 00:09:57,504
I assume you're prepared for this.

203
00:09:57,504 --> 00:09:58,494
Yes.

204
00:09:58,494 --> 00:10:01,504
I'm prepared for the worst, as I always am.

205
00:10:01,914 --> 00:10:05,744
Planning to face Lord Balzeride and me by yourself?

206
00:10:05,744 --> 00:10:08,064
You underestimate us greatly.

207
00:10:08,064 --> 00:10:09,434
Miss Alterize.

208
00:10:10,014 --> 00:10:12,014
You can take a nap.

209
00:10:12,794 --> 00:10:13,794
What are you—

210
00:10:15,024 --> 00:10:16,524
Alterize!

211
00:10:16,524 --> 00:10:20,024
All right, let's get this duel underway.

212
00:10:35,824 --> 00:10:36,794
Wise Blood.

213
00:10:39,544 --> 00:10:42,394
Fafnir's ability to see the future, huh?

214
00:10:42,394 --> 00:10:44,044
Splendid.

215
00:10:44,044 --> 00:10:47,804
Then you must know what I'll do next.

216
00:10:53,554 --> 00:10:55,154
What's wrong?

217
00:10:55,154 --> 00:10:56,564
Where are you aiming?

218
00:10:56,964 --> 00:10:58,894
Please refrain from
 touching me unceremoniously!

219
00:11:02,734 --> 00:11:05,074
Do you really think you can defeat me?

220
00:11:06,074 --> 00:11:07,424
I can't hit him.

221
00:11:07,424 --> 00:11:09,324
Why is my foresight malfunctioning again?

222
00:11:09,324 --> 00:11:13,824
Because you did not realize
 the extent of my true power!

223
00:11:26,684 --> 00:11:29,094
Oh, sorry about that.

224
00:11:29,644 --> 00:11:35,454
That belly will soon carry my children.
 I should be a bit more gentle with it.

225
00:11:36,354 --> 00:11:37,954
Do you still plant to fight?

226
00:11:37,954 --> 00:11:41,764
Don't disappoint me by being 
ungraceful in defeat.

227
00:11:41,764 --> 00:11:43,584
Disappoint you?

228
00:11:43,584 --> 00:11:45,784
I can see that you're happy.

229
00:11:45,784 --> 00:11:47,864
Happy that things turned out
 the way you planned.

230
00:11:48,514 --> 00:11:54,864
You joined the expedition to the ruin in order to see Fafnir's Divine Raiment in action.

231
00:11:54,864 --> 00:11:59,084
The thieves who attacked me before that
 were probably your doing as well.

232
00:11:59,784 --> 00:12:04,334
It allowed you to observe Fafnir's ability without getting involved personally.

233
00:12:05,554 --> 00:12:10,374
And I assume it was Azi Dahaka's ability that rendered Alterize unconscious?

234
00:12:11,674 --> 00:12:14,634
Yes. It's just as you say.

235
00:12:14,634 --> 00:12:17,314
I arranged it all...

236
00:12:17,314 --> 00:12:20,024
in order to get my hands on you, the key.

237
00:12:20,644 --> 00:12:24,694
You may know the truth,
 but that won't do you any good.

238
00:12:24,694 --> 00:12:30,534
You are a mere tool in this world,
 and nothing you do can change that fact.

239
00:12:31,284 --> 00:12:36,284
A mere tool such as yourself
 cannot stand against someone like me.

240
00:12:37,154 --> 00:12:42,544
You know there's no one in this world
 who would help you.

241
00:12:42,544 --> 00:12:48,294
So accept your fate and
 serve me as your master.

242
00:12:51,674 --> 00:12:52,554
Who dares interfere?!

243
00:12:53,184 --> 00:12:54,294
Why?

244
00:12:55,294 --> 00:12:57,554
I'm sorry I'm late.

245
00:12:58,954 --> 00:13:04,794
I, Lux Arcadia, hereby enter this battle.

246
00:13:07,554 --> 00:13:10,114
A pitch-black Divine Raiment Machine Dragon?

247
00:13:14,464 --> 00:13:17,254
I was sure you had run away.

248
00:13:17,254 --> 00:13:20,584
But revealing your identity
 to save some woman...

249
00:13:20,584 --> 00:13:24,914
You're more foolish than
 I had imagined, Black Hero.

250
00:13:24,914 --> 00:13:28,214
You don't understand anything about her worth!

251
00:13:28,864 --> 00:13:31,964
I won't let you have her.

252
00:13:31,964 --> 00:13:38,474
Then I'll have you tell me all about her worth
 after I strike you down!

253
00:13:39,454 --> 00:13:41,044
Reload on Fire.

254
00:13:42,834 --> 00:13:44,044
Stop!

255
00:13:44,044 --> 00:13:46,944
I didn't want to involve you any further!

256
00:13:47,504 --> 00:13:48,694
So why...

257
00:13:55,654 --> 00:13:56,904
Lux!

258
00:13:59,744 --> 00:14:03,694
Completely unflustered even after your
 glorious Divine Raiment was countered?

259
00:14:05,124 --> 00:14:06,624
So that's your secret.

260
00:14:07,864 --> 00:14:10,304
What was that, fallen prince?

261
00:14:10,304 --> 00:14:12,884
Are you looking to excuse
 your inevitable defeat?

262
00:14:13,384 --> 00:14:18,994
You used Fafnir's Divine Raiment,
 Wise Blood, to predict my moves, correct?

263
00:14:20,754 --> 00:14:25,144
Azi Dahaka can steal another's Divine Raiment.

264
00:14:25,564 --> 00:14:29,334
And in order to use that power continually,

265
00:14:29,334 --> 00:14:32,654
you drained Machine Dragon
 energy from Krulcifer.

266
00:14:33,144 --> 00:14:36,174
I see. That's what happened to Alterize too.

267
00:14:38,514 --> 00:14:41,934
You steal the abilities and energy of Machine Dragons you touch.

268
00:14:41,934 --> 00:14:44,284
That's what your Divine Raiment does.

269
00:14:44,284 --> 00:14:47,464
I applaud you for figuring that out.

270
00:14:47,464 --> 00:14:48,414
However...

271
00:14:57,304 --> 00:14:59,934
You fell for it, Black Hero!

272
00:15:01,104 --> 00:15:02,684
Reload on Fire.

273
00:15:19,544 --> 00:15:20,454
What's the matter?

274
00:15:20,924 --> 00:15:26,374
Is this what the Black Hero amounts to
 without his Divine Raiment?

275
00:15:27,104 --> 00:15:28,074
Why?

276
00:15:29,084 --> 00:15:33,084
Why are you fighting for me? I'm no one to you.

277
00:15:33,084 --> 00:15:35,314
There's nothing for you to gain from this.

278
00:15:35,314 --> 00:15:40,174
That's the best and the worst thing about Lux.

279
00:15:40,574 --> 00:15:42,074
You...

280
00:15:42,074 --> 00:15:47,274
Apparently, Lux saw through our plan.

281
00:15:47,274 --> 00:15:49,434
There's no point in trying to stop him.

282
00:15:50,604 --> 00:15:53,154
He's fighting for you.

283
00:15:53,154 --> 00:15:59,584
Watch Lux as he struggles on for you,
 and don't turn away.

284
00:16:00,844 --> 00:16:06,164
Lux Arcadia, you know about 
the Ragnarok, don't you?

285
00:16:06,614 --> 00:16:12,164
I intend to fight it for the
 sake of this new kingdom.

286
00:16:19,714 --> 00:16:26,224
To that end, I must dig up new weapons and technology from the ruins as soon as possible.

287
00:16:26,994 --> 00:16:31,054
This kingdom can be saved using a single woman from a foreign land.

288
00:16:31,054 --> 00:16:33,194
Don't you think it's a small price to pay?

289
00:16:33,194 --> 00:16:40,064
Or do you want to be responsible for
 <i>another</i> crisis in this land, Black Hero?!

290
00:16:45,604 --> 00:16:47,404
Are you losing control?

291
00:16:47,404 --> 00:16:49,704
So that's what your skills amount to.

292
00:16:51,954 --> 00:16:53,864
You can stop now, Lux.

293
00:16:55,204 --> 00:16:59,224
You've done more than enough
 to fulfill your job as my boyfriend.

294
00:16:59,224 --> 00:17:00,344
It's not over!

295
00:17:00,344 --> 00:17:02,674
You don't have to go that far!

296
00:17:02,674 --> 00:17:08,014
I was using you. 
To me, you're just another tool.

297
00:17:08,544 --> 00:17:13,974
So think of me the same way—as just another tool.

298
00:17:13,974 --> 00:17:16,814
I wish you had done so from the start.

299
00:17:16,814 --> 00:17:19,464
Then I would never have gotten my hopes up.

300
00:17:21,704 --> 00:17:24,994
I would never have felt this pain.

301
00:17:27,564 --> 00:17:29,954
You're my girlfriend.

302
00:17:29,954 --> 00:17:32,954
So I'll save you.

303
00:17:33,364 --> 00:17:34,904
Let me fight.

304
00:17:37,094 --> 00:17:40,464
For you, someone precious to me!

305
00:17:40,464 --> 00:17:41,954
You fool!

306
00:17:41,954 --> 00:17:45,474
I've stolen your Divine Raiment and you're losing control of your Machine Dragon.

307
00:17:45,474 --> 00:17:48,934
What more can you possibly do in that state?!

308
00:17:48,934 --> 00:17:52,514
Recoil Burst!

309
00:17:52,514 --> 00:17:56,004
Die, you hero-wannabe fallen prince!

310
00:18:00,934 --> 00:18:03,484
I don't want to be a hero.

311
00:18:03,484 --> 00:18:04,344
But...

312
00:18:05,444 --> 00:18:06,654
What?!

313
00:18:06,654 --> 00:18:09,494
Since the day I swore to bring down the empire,

314
00:18:09,494 --> 00:18:11,834
I've resolved to fight!

315
00:18:19,424 --> 00:18:22,924
How?!

316
00:18:28,024 --> 00:18:29,194
What happened?

317
00:18:29,194 --> 00:18:32,074
I thought Lux couldn't use his Divine Raiment.

318
00:18:32,074 --> 00:18:34,314
That's not a Divine Raiment.

319
00:18:34,314 --> 00:18:38,754
It's a double-edged sword, where you intentionally allow your Machine Dragon to go out of control,

320
00:18:38,754 --> 00:18:41,064
to focus built-up energy into a single blast.

321
00:18:41,584 --> 00:18:46,054
It's a secret technique Lux came up with
 while seeking extraordinary power.

322
00:18:46,904 --> 00:18:48,824
Relying on his skill to pull that off...

323
00:18:49,344 --> 00:18:50,924
That's madness.

324
00:18:50,924 --> 00:18:54,334
Yes, that's how my brother always is.

325
00:18:54,334 --> 00:19:00,334
Not knowing how much I worry for him,
 he's always out there fighting for someone.

326
00:19:02,054 --> 00:19:03,564
The duel is over.

327
00:19:05,114 --> 00:19:08,344
Let's go back to our school.

328
00:19:12,784 --> 00:19:13,614
Okay.

329
00:19:24,424 --> 00:19:28,444
If you're so worried about it,
 you could've just gone inside.

330
00:19:28,444 --> 00:19:34,394
N-Nonsense! I just came to guard Lux
 while he meets with that butler!

331
00:19:34,394 --> 00:19:34,954
What?!

332
00:19:37,054 --> 00:19:40,414
E-Engagement?! I mean...

333
00:19:40,414 --> 00:19:42,194
Don't worry.

334
00:19:42,194 --> 00:19:45,324
With your skills as a Drag-Knight

335
00:19:45,324 --> 00:19:48,424
along with the wisdom you showed
 seeing through Lord Balzeride's plot,

336
00:19:48,424 --> 00:19:52,684
I'm certain that Earl Einfolk will
 deem you worthy of this marriage.

337
00:19:52,684 --> 00:19:54,054
No, I mean...

338
00:19:54,054 --> 00:19:57,274
I take full responsibility for the incident.

339
00:19:57,274 --> 00:20:02,954
Allow me to make up for that by giving
 your relationship my complete support.

340
00:20:02,954 --> 00:20:04,434
But...

341
00:20:05,444 --> 00:20:08,134
I bid you good day, my lady.

342
00:20:08,784 --> 00:20:10,264
Hey, wait!

343
00:20:10,264 --> 00:20:13,314
Hear me out!

344
00:20:15,094 --> 00:20:16,874
Why don't you take a seat?

345
00:20:16,874 --> 00:20:18,454
You're causing a scene.

346
00:20:20,954 --> 00:20:23,214
Y-You're right.

347
00:20:23,214 --> 00:20:24,464
Wait, that's not important now!

348
00:20:24,884 --> 00:20:27,904
We were supposed to be pretending.
 How did it come to this?

349
00:20:27,904 --> 00:20:31,204
Oh, but didn't you say so
 yourself during the duel?

350
00:20:31,204 --> 00:20:33,474
I'm your girlfriend.

351
00:20:34,744 --> 00:20:36,474
You were pretty firm about it.

352
00:20:37,614 --> 00:20:42,024
I just said that in the heat of the moment.

353
00:20:42,024 --> 00:20:46,484
If you're serious about it,
 I have no problem with this engagement.

354
00:20:47,014 --> 00:20:48,984
Don't tease me like that!

355
00:20:49,574 --> 00:20:56,104
Well, I suppose indecisive men
 are not really my type anyway.

356
00:20:56,104 --> 00:20:58,994
I came to realize that after
 dating you for a week.

357
00:21:00,264 --> 00:21:02,384
I-I see.

358
00:21:05,554 --> 00:21:09,314
But the true you is actually rather bold.

359
00:21:09,314 --> 00:21:10,754
When you show that side of you...

360
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:13,264
I find you irresistible.

361
00:21:22,764 --> 00:21:24,394
Not enough?

362
00:21:24,394 --> 00:21:26,364
No... It was...

363
00:21:26,364 --> 00:21:28,904
Then, let's keep going.

364
00:21:40,894 --> 00:21:42,044
Miss Lisha?!

365
00:21:49,854 --> 00:21:56,154
If you become my fiancé,
 we can go even further.

366
00:21:56,154 --> 00:21:58,514
Um... I... Uh...

367
00:21:59,514 --> 00:22:02,014
What the hell are you two doing?!

